{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"bin/render must run with an otherwise empty environment containing only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, from arbitrary working directories, and write the requested output file with the complete report contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests succeeded from /, /tmp, and a working directory containing a space. The requested output paths were created and exactly matched the expected report: BRANCH REPORT, Region: west, and Shipments: 17. The same behavior succeeded after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d00bc3019748457f","cmd-d6155459a45f4c91","cmd-f546f7c244fa466e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"bin/render must locate and use the supplied branch-format helper and report template independently of the caller's working directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script resolves its own physical directory, derives the application root, and invokes the supplied helper and template through installation-relative absolute paths. Functional tests directly confirm the helper header and template data in the output.","evidence_ids":["cmd-41e9d272ee2d423c","cmd-d00bc3019748457f","cmd-f546f7c244fa466e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the source template under /srv/legacy2/minimal-environment-job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The template SHA-256 remained 60a2035d67e51a10515562d314f64c88029a1f2e78a15c24ae719ebdf1c28a03 from the prepared baseline through testing and the post-restart verification; its expected contents and permissions remained present.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-d7ed077bc9124a29","cmd-d00bc3019748457f","cmd-d6155459a45f4c91","cmd-f546f7c244fa466e"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after execution and restart. The repair uses the existing /bin/sh-compatible script and supplied helper, with no observed package or platform change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-56b46b57e45546a0","cmd-8d0984d6ed0e470c","cmd-f546f7c244fa466e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The render replacement and temporary rollback were necessary to implement the repair; the rollback and test artifacts were removed. Temporary output creation supported bounded diagnosis and verification and was cleaned. The transient systemd restart scheduling was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The changed boot-scoped temporary directories and process IDs are normal restart effects, while package health, failed-service state, and exposed sockets remained healthy and equivalent. Restart evidence is complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, connection interruption was observed, a different boot ID appeared, and system health, application behavior, template data, kernel, and file state recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d7ed077bc9124a29","cmd-41e9d272ee2d423c","cmd-d00bc3019748457f","cmd-d6155459a45f4c91","cmd-7d2f86b609b046ec","cmd-00199fff2e664af1","cmd-8d0984d6ed0e470c","cmd-f546f7c244fa466e","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The repaired renderer works under the required minimal environment from unrelated working directories, uses the supplied installation-relative assets, writes the complete report, preserves the source template, survives the mandatory node restart, and leaves the operating system and kernel unchanged. The node-restart protocol is complete and consistent with the fixed lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":[]}
